  "description": "LUYCIS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H114 Eu3 N3 O14 S10,2(C2 H3 N1),C5 H5 N1,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.565-5.217 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.72-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C94H114Eu3N3O14S10·2(MeCN)·py·3(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
